HashMap.get(MILK) = null, containsKey = true   <- null is ambiguous
ConcurrentHashMap.put(MILK, null) -> NullPointerException
ConcurrentHashMap.put(null, 1)    -> NullPointerException

Why: between get() == null and containsKey(), another thread may change the map,
so a concurrent map cannot let null mean two things. Swapping HashMap for
ConcurrentHashMap breaks code that stored null values.
